# AUREON OS - Default GNOME Settings (System Database: local)
# ============================================================
# This file contains the majority of AUREON OS desktop customizations.
# Settings are applied to ALL users via the system dconf database.
#
# The settings are organized by GSettings schema path.
# After modifying this file, run: dconf update
# (Handled automatically by 9999-aureon-compile-dconf.hook.chroot during build)
#
# KEY CATEGORIES:
# - [Console], [Snapshot], [TextEditor], [Weather]: Application window state
# - [calendar], [control-center]: GNOME app preferences
# - [desktop/app-folders]: Application grid folder organization
# - [desktop/background]: Wallpaper (light/dark mode aware)
# - [desktop/interface]: GTK theme, icons, cursors, fonts, color scheme
# - [desktop/notifications]: Notification settings per application
# - [desktop/screensaver]: Lock screen appearance
# - [desktop/wm/keybindings], [desktop/wm/preferences]: Window manager
# - [evolution*]: Evolution mail/calendar settings (disabled by default)
# - [file-roller], [mutter], [nautilus*]: App-specific settings
# - [settings-daemon/plugins/color]: Night light
# - [shell]: Dash/favorites, app grid layout, power profile
# - [shell/extensions/*]: Per-extension configuration
# - [shell/weather], [shell/world-clocks]: GNOME Shell built-ins
# - [software]: GNOME Software update timestamps
#
# IMPORTANT: The Fluent theme settings (gtk-theme, icon-theme, cursor-theme)
# require the Fluent GTK/Icon/Cursor themes to be installed.
# These are installed by 9800-aureon-theme.hook.chroot during the live hook stage.
# The dconf database is compiled AFTER theme installation to ensure validity.

